      "stop_during_wait": "STOPPED",
      "rule": "Agent roles (the reference Actor and the native smolagents adapters) keep rule v1: at most one blind retry of the identical request, only when no answer arrived (a connection error, a timeout, or HTTP 503 after a one-second wait). FaultLab's own lab roles in this Learn campaign (Explorer discovery and challenge selections, Mechanic diagnosis and candidate requests) may re-send the identical request up to 3 times, after waits of 5 s, 20 s and 60 s, only when no answer arrived (connection error, timeout, HTTP 503), and at most 12 times in the whole campaign; during discovery the declared Explorer retry bound also applies. An answer, even an empty or malformed one, is never retried, and neither is any other HTTP status or an authentication, configuration or model-identity failure. Every retry is charged in model calls, tokens and dollars before it is sent, from unreserved campaign capacity only. A Stop during a wait ends the campaign STOPPED and nothing more is sent. If every allowed retry fails, the campaign ends ERROR as before and says how many retries were tried. Separate studies started on the campaign keep rule v1."
